OL,3,GNEWSAFootball club apologises over
OL,4,Aon-pitch 'assault'
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn amateur football club in West Sussex
OL,7,Fhas apologised after one of its players
OL,8,Freportedly assaulted two opposing team
OL,9,Fmembers, leaving one requiring hospital
OL,10,Ftreatment.
OL,12,FSaturday's match in Easebourne, between
OL,13,FMidhurst and Easebourne FC (MEFC) and
OL,14,Fvisitors Emsworth Town, had to be
OL,15,Fabandoned after about 20 minutes
OL,16,Ffollowing what the home side called a
OL,17,F"completely unprovoked attack".
OL,19,FMEFC said its player had been left with
OL,20,F"severe damage" to the inside of his
OL,21,Fmouth, a broken bone in his jaw and "a
OL,22,Fhigh chance of requiring surgery".
OL,23,APub: 03-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
